            <ArticleTitle>Imaging of acute small-bowel obstruction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1036-44</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">The objective of this pictorial essay is to review the different imaging techniques used for diagnosing small-bowel obstruction.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Small-bowel obstruction is a common presentation, for which safe and effective management depends on a rapid and accurate diagnosis. Conventional radiographs remain the first line of imaging. CT is used increasingly more because it provides essential diagnostic information not apparent from radiographs. MRI may play a role in the future as technology improves and it becomes more readily available.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
